lunduke-about (0.9-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * CPU core and thread counts, and each extra GPU name, wrap inside the
    stats column. A 36-character ellipsis no longer hides them. A long OS
    name still ellipsizes so the window stays 520px wide.
  * A loopback TCP display (localhost, 127.0.0.1, tcp/, [::1]) names the X
    server from the listening port in /proc/net/tcp and tcp6. A zero
    SO_PEERCRED pid is not "Unknown GPU". A root server whose fd directory
    is unreadable is named from the port owner's uid and comm.
  * The application list scrollbar uses the classic blue thumb. The theme
    outside this window is unchanged.
  * Enter activates the focused row's Force Close menu. The tooltip names
    Shift+F10.
  * Naming a display gives up when its socket accepts and never speaks, so
    a wedged X server cannot hang the window or the tests.
  * Meson project version remains 0.9.

